 beautiful and for a second you feel like you're in the Caribbean. We sat at the bar and looked at the HUGE menu - including Happy Hour specials. We decided to order the Latitude 29 signature drink and the 504 drink as per other Yelp-er's suggestions. Loved them both! They serve the drinks i..."},{"business_id":"7D5-a53BLau19RpMu-L3zg","review_id":"Fu--UsO-3uZgI06OS14oJw","date":"2015-03-31T18:58:07","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9387622475624084,"text_excerpt":"My visit to Beachbum Berry's Latitude 29 was about 5 or 6 months in the making. I wanted to visit this place as soon as I first heard about it and after hearing all the raves, my excitement had reached it's peak by the time I finally set foot here. Something you may or may not know about me: I LOVE tiki drinks. Come on, how can you go wrong with fruit, sugar and spices? Sadly, it seemed like every time I had plans to visit LAT 29, something came up. I finally made it here and my experience did not disappoint. We stopped into this cute restaurant and bar located in the Bienville House Hotel. Oh yeah, they serve food too! I didn't know either until about a month or two ago. I'm going to get..."},{"business_id":"7D5-a53BLau19RpMu-L3zg","review_id":"lGHuDcNEsrVH_bhf7B4ZyA","date":"2015-04-17T03:44:46","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.937889814376831,"text_excerpt":"I've had a solo excursion here at the bar as well as a 5 person nosh sesh, and both times were spot-on! Some die-hard tiki interior designer really had their way with this place because it is tiki from head to toe with very little recognizable aspects from when it was Iris. The bar and restaurant are separated by a wall that kinda cuts out some of my people watching ability but probably helps me focus more on the peeps I'm with. They also incorporated a plug and USB plugs in the booths on the restaurant side! Drink/food pics fa' days (but please no flash, thanks). I was in between engagements one night, and decided to belly up to the bar 